Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:00:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] nemotron: --mtp-drafts and --mtp-confidence set a lone
 CUDA stream's MTP depth

The CUDA server refused both. --mtp-drafts now caps a lone stream's chain (0 serves without drafts) and
--mtp-confidence replaces the cost rule's cut with a cumulative-confidence floor; both reach cuda_lone's depth rule,
and copied continuations and concurrent lanes keep their policies. They are refused before device work for other
families, past the window's drafts, or outside [0, 1]. A draft never changes a reply, only how many a round verifies.
